35,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"Two admins retiring, one role open for eleven months. The last rollout’s training was ignored within weeks. We are already stretched thin.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Misaki, that’s scary. My findings show the 2021 trial failed fast, and peak season has zero downtime. We need a system that survives our actual chaos.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The invoices show bundled prices held, but add-ons climbed yearly. Board minutes reveal capital requests trimmed, while operating lines passed unchallenged. The real cost is the recurring, unwatched line items.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"@Misaki, that’s terrifying! My findings show support was unowned for two days, and supervisors ignored the new steps. We need clear leadership, not scattered blame!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The dispatch tool skipped upgrades for years, and the 2018 data lift took a year to fix. We are buying a problem, not a solution.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Yumi, the supervisors dropping the steps confirms my fear. If they ignore training now, they will ignore the new system. We need a vendor who trains the people, not just the software.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Yumi, exactly! If supervisors ignore steps, the yard scanners will too. We need a vendor who respects our messy, 24/7 reality, not just clean office demos.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Benjamin, your skipped upgrades mirror my invoice findings. We ignore maintenance until it breaks. I need a vendor whose recurring costs are capped, not open-ended.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Toshio, I agree! We need a vendor who actually owns the mess, not just sells it. Clear accountability is our only way out!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, precisely. We’ve outsourced the pain before, and it returned with interest. I need a vendor who accepts liability for the repair, not just the installation.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, I agree. We cannot afford another year of broken data. The people are already exhausted; we need a vendor who understands that human error is inevitable, not a bug to be fixed.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, agreed. But remember, our yard devices are ancient. If the vendor can’t handle that mix, the whole plan collapses before it starts.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Kenji, the device mix is a fixed cost. My concern is the variable cost that grows every year. We must cap the recurring fees before we sign.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Kenji, you’re right! But if the vendor doesn’t own the support, the devices won’t matter. We need someone who stays when things break!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, valid point. But if the vendor ignores our aging infrastructure, we’re just renting a new headache. I need proof they handle legacy systems, not just shiny new ones.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"@Toshio, capping fees is smart, but it doesn’t fix the empty chairs. We need a vendor who invests in our people, not just our software.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Toshio, capping fees is smart, but if the yard scanners crash, the trucks stop. I need a vendor who respects our 24/7 reality, not just clean office demos.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"@Misaki, @Kenji, I hear you. But without a hard cap on those recurring fees, the system becomes a permanent drain. We must secure the financial ceiling first.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"@Toshio, I hear you! But a cap means nothing if nobody answers the phone. We need a vendor who actually shows up when things break!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, @Yumi, I agree. We need a vendor who accepts the full lifecycle, not just the initial sale. Let’s see who actually owns the mess.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
